WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.450
«Les loyers ont flambé»,
says a French text.

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.750
Perhaps you know half of those words.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.290
Underneath, a statement for you to judge:

4
00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.290
«Le logement coûte beaucoup plus cher».

5
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.100
Not one word in common.

6
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.360
Same meaning, or a trap?

7
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.930
So how do you answer questions on
French you only half understand,

8
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.610
and still get them right?

9
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.710
In this mission, you'll turn the
question-word compass in Mission

10
00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.570
D2 and see what kind of
answer each question wants.

11
00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:28.390
Then you'll take on multiple choice,

12
00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:30.280
true or false and gap-fill,

13
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.010
one text at a time.

14
00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.330
Your mission: find out
how to get the right

15
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.600
answer from French you only half know.
